<div class="xfer" data-xfer>
  <h2>1. On the device that has your progress</h2>
  <p>Copy this code. It holds every tick and counter saved in this browser: <b data-xfer-sum></b>.</p>
  <textarea data-xfer-out readonly rows="4" aria-label="Your progress code"></textarea>
  <p><button type="button" class="btn primary" data-xfer-copy>Copy code</button></p>

  <h2>2. On the other device</h2>
  <p>Open this page there, paste the code and press Add. Send it to yourself any way you like: a note, an email, a message.</p>
  <textarea data-xfer-in rows="4" placeholder="Paste a progress code here" aria-label="Paste a progress code"></textarea>
  <p><button type="button" class="btn" data-xfer-load>Add to this device</button></p>
  <p class="xfer-msg" data-xfer-msg role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

  <h2>What happens</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Nothing is removed.</b> Anything ticked on either device ends up ticked, and each counter keeps the higher number.</li>
    <li><b>It is a copy, not a sync.</b> Do it again whenever you want the other device to catch up.</li>
    <li><b>Nothing leaves your browser.</b> The code is your progress written out as text. There is no account and no server.</li>
  </ul>
</div>
